{
  "analysis": "The sed command didn't fully work because the pattern included special characters. The compilation failed because `-msoft-float` requires `gnu/stubs-o32_soft.h` which is missing from the cross-compiler's glibc headers. I need to either create that missing header or avoid using system glibc headers in vm_runtime.c. I also need to check whether the Doom source files themselves will have the same issue with -msoft-float.",
  "plan": "First, fix the remaining _FILE_minimal references in vm_runtime.c. Then check what glibc stubs headers exist and create the missing stubs-o32_soft.h if needed. After that, test compiling vm_runtime.c and a Doom source file with -msoft-float.",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "cd /app/doomgeneric/doomgeneric && sed -i '/struct _FILE_minimal/d' vm_runtime.c && nl -ba vm_runtime.c | sed -n '466,484p'\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "SYSROOT=$(mipsel-linux-gnu-gcc -print-sysroot); echo \"sysroot=$SYSROOT\"; ls -la \"$SYSROOT/usr/include/gnu/\" 2>/dev/null | grep stubs; cat \"$SYSROOT/usr/include/gnu/stubs-o32_hard.h\" 2>/dev/null | head -20; echo \"---\"; cat \"$SYSROOT/usr/include/gnu/stubs.h\" 2>/dev/null | head -20\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "echo '#include <stdio.h>\\nint x;' > /tmp/stest.c && mipsel-linux-gnu-gcc -O2 -EL -march=mips32 -msoft-float -mno-abicalls -fno-pic -ffreestanding -nostdlib -fno-builtin -c /tmp/stest.c -o /tmp/stest.o 2>&1 | head -20; echo \"exit=${PIPESTATUS[0]}\"\n",
      "duration": 1.0
    }
  ]
}
